# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation policy (Task 1)
# Only two documentation artefacts are public: README.md and the final report
# PDF. AI_USAGE.md is kept on disk but excluded from Git by a rule below. All
# other internal documentation was moved to
# ../terrashift_local_archive/archived_docs_2026-11-22/ and must not re-enter
# this repository. These rules are path-specific on purpose: they must never
# hide configuration, schemas, manifests, source, the AI usage record or the
# report PDF.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/PLAN.md
/docs/*.md
# The canonical, maintained source for the technical report.
!/docs/report.md
/docs/*.pdf
!/docs/report_2026-11-22.pdf
/docs/decisions/
/docs/reviews/
/review/*/*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packaging, build and cache hygiene (Task 3)
# Path-specific rules only. Deliberately NOT ignored anywhere: *.onnx, *.pt, *.tif,
# *.jp2, *.csv, *.json, *.yaml, *.geojson — the repository tracks schemas, manifests,
# label indexes and model artefacts that share those extensions.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/
*.egg-info/

# test, lint and type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# local logs and temporary files
*.log
logs/

# Python version pin written by some tools on this machine only
.python-version

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment artefacts (Task 3, confirmed: `git ls-files experiments` returns 0)
# 706 MB of checkpoints, prediction .npz files and harness scratch from the abandoned
# OSCD architecture sweep. Never part of the source distribution; the results that matter
# are summarised in the report. Ignoring this does not delete anything on disk.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/experiments/

# internal AI usage record, withheld from publication
/AI_USAGE.md
